5:1).","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":9,"text":"3. strangers—perhaps Ziphites.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"oppressors—literally, \"terrible ones\" (Isa 13:11; 25:3).","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"Such were Saul and his army.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"not set … them—acted as atheists, without God's fear (compare Ps 16:8).","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"(Compare Ps 30:10).","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"with them—on their side, and for me (compare Ps 46:11).","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":16,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":17,"text":"He shall … evil—or, \"Evil shall return on\" (Ps 7:16) my enemies or watchers, that is, to do me evil (Ps 6:7).","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"in thy truth—Thy verified promise.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":20,"text":"I will freely, &c.—or, present a freewill offering (Le 7:16; Nu 15:3).","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"7. mine eye … desire—(compare Ps 59:10; 112:8), expresses satisfaction in beholding the overthrow of his enemies as those of God, without implying any selfish or unholy feeling (compare Ps 52:6, 7).","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":54}}